Falsifies `environment_contract::verification::field_bytes_never_panics_for_any_length_byte`.

The defect: `field_bytes` trusts the length byte and no longer compares it with the field's maximum, so a
length of 255 in `TERM` slices past the end of the page.

Expected to fail: the slice's index-out-of-bounds check inside `field_bytes`, at any length over the
maximum of 24, and the harness's `assert!(read.is_none())` for the same lengths.

diff --git a/crates/environment_contract/src/lib.rs b/crates/environment_contract/src/lib.rs
--- a/crates/environment_contract/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/environment_contract/src/lib.rs
@@ -345,10 +345,10 @@
     maximum_bytes: usize,
 ) -> Option<&[u8]> {
     let n = *page.get(length_offset)? as usize;
-    if n == 0 || n > maximum_bytes {
+    if n == 0 {
         return None;
     }
-    page.get(value_offset..value_offset.checked_add(n)?)
+    Some(&page[value_offset..value_offset + n])
 }
 
